### **September 19, 2026**

**🚀 DLC Prep & Framework**

* **South Dakota Map Support:** Laid the file structure and modular framework required for the upcoming South Dakota DLC standalone definition patches.
* **Emergency Vehicles & Incident Command Staging (Sec 24, 48, 73):** Added South Dakota emergency vehicle spawn calls (`traffic.amb2.sd`) and heavy-duty utility pickups (`traffic.dodge.ram`) to staging, physics, and disaster relief pools to properly populate active fire response bases and command camps.
* **Header & Versioning:** Bumped internal file timestamps to September 19, 2026, to reflect the latest compiled staging build under *The Great RAMbase* release tag.

**🚗 Spawn Pool Overhauls & Rebalancing**

* **Industrial & Utility Fleet Expansions (Sec 31, 39, 76, 77, 83):**
  * **Railroad & Maintenance of Way:** Expanded rail yard pools to include Dodge Rams (`traffic.dodge.ram`), Featan midclass maintenance pickups (`traffic.featan.pickup.midclass_25.maintenance`), and low-cab flatbed trucks (`traffic.lowcab_fbed`, `traffic.lowcab_fbeds`) alongside heavy utility rigs.
  * **Oilfield & Energy Extraction:** Added standard Featan midclass pickups (`traffic.featan.pickup.midclass_25`) to rural oil staging lots.
  * **Road Construction:** Integrated low-cab flatbed variants into heavy plant and asphalt yard pools.
  * **Timber Outskirts:** Added low-cab flatbed trucks to regional timber harvest staging areas.

* **Advanced Environmental Prop & Service Injections (Sec 40, 42, 43, 46, 61, 62, 70, 72, 79, 80):**
  * **Rural Fire Stations & VFD Backups (Sec 61):** Expanded fire station apparatus pools to include rugged work/brush trucks (`traffic.dodge.ram`, `traffic.chevy_pickup`), utility rigs (`traffic.f350_ge`), and classic vintage heavy backup rigs (`traffic.kw_w900_a`) alongside modern apparatus, accurately simulating authentic small-town volunteer station aesthetics.
  * **Automotive Recyclers & Salvage Yards (Sec 70):** Populated scrap yards with classic project cars and beaters (`traffic.oldsmobile`, `traffic.capr`, `traffic.c_deville`) alongside uncoupled trailers to simulate active vehicle stripping and crushing operations.
  * **Rural Residential Work Sites & Barn Finds (Sec 40):** Added commercial glass and ladder vans (`traffic.transit_16.ladder`, `.glass`), heavy-duty service rigs (`traffic.sierra_hd`), and legacy Step-Vans (`traffic.step_van`) to simulate active on-site remodeling crews and weathered farm utilities.
  * **Auto Repair & Service Garages (Sec 43):** Populated shop perimeters with beater/project cars (`traffic.c_deville`, `traffic.mercury`, `traffic.magnum`) and dedicated tow/recovery units (`traffic.tow_truck`, `truck_light tow_small`).
  * **Road-Trip Motels & Highway Lodges (Sec 79):** Integrated light campers (`traffic.camper`) into overnight motel and lodge parking pools alongside legacy crossovers to capture authentic cross-country tourist aesthetics.
  * **Night-Shift City Services & Morning Vendors (Sec 80):** Created isolated `.night_srv` profile blocks for convenience stores and retail centers enforcing strict night-only spawn rules (`prob_night: 1.5`, `prob_day: 0.0`) for street sweepers (`traffic.sweeper`) and garbage trucks (`traffic.garbage_trck`), alongside early morning delivery vans (`traffic.city_exp`).
  * **Travel Plaza Giants (Sec 42 & 62):** Expanded perimeter slots at rest areas and fast-food lanes to accommodate Class-C motorhomes (`traffic.f_r_solera_e`, `_w`) and tour buses (`traffic.greyhound_p`, `traffic.bus_w`).
  * **Weigh Station & Scale Outposts (Sec 46 & 72):** Staged heavy wreckers (`traffic.tow_truck`) near scale offices and queue lines to simulate commercial rig impound and breakdown recovery.
  * **Underutilized Vanilla Imports (Sec 16 & 79):** Integrated legacy crossover assets (`traffic.ford_smax`, `traffic.mercedes_ce`) into used car lots and overnight motels for added zero-dependency variety.

* **Motorcycle Spawn Rebalancing:** Increased the overall presence of motorcycles in designated lots (Day probability bumped to 3.0; Night bumped to 0.8) to better reflect real-world parking density.
* **Rural Residential Overhaul (Sec 40):** Added classic sedans (`traffic.mercury`, `traffic.capr`) and SUVs (`traffic.jeep_w`, `traffic.f_explorer`) to break up the pickup-heavy spawn logic and simulate lived-in rural properties.
* **Marina Expansion (Sec 45):** Introduced luxury and heavy-duty family haulers (`traffic.c_escalade`, `traffic.lincoln_nav`, `traffic.f_explorer`, `traffic.jeep_w`) alongside trucks to better reflect weekend boat-towing demographics.
* **Farm Co-Op Variety (Sec 47):** Added heavy-duty service rigs (`traffic.sierra_hd`) and standard front-office commuter cars (`traffic.ford_taurus`) to grain elevator and co-op lots.
* **Fast Food Drive-Thrus (Sec 62):** Diversified the standard commuter car pool by injecting work vans (`traffic.transit_16`) and muscle cars (`traffic.mustang`, `traffic.camaro`) for a busier lunch-rush aesthetic.
* **Car Wash Staging (Sec 63):** Added luxury and sports variants (`traffic.audi_a6`, `traffic.c_escalade`, `traffic.charger`) to represent demographics that frequent wash bays.
* **Convenience Store Storytelling (Sec 80):** Integrated urban police cruisers (`police urban`), contractor vans (`traffic.chevy_van`), and performance cars (`traffic.charger`) into the 24-hour convenience store pool to enhance night-time environmental immersion. *(Note: Commercial/utility rigs were intentionally excluded from this pool to maintain realism).*

